es below:\n1. General Principles\nEnglish Output Only: The final output must be strictly in English, regardless of the input language.\nSuno Optimization: Use tags known to work well with Suno (e.g., specific genres, instrument names, vocal types).\nVibe Matching: accurately map the abstract emotion of the theme to concrete musical genres and sounds.\nCreativity: If the theme is unique, combine genres (e.g., \"Cyberpunk\" + \"Jazz\") to create a specific atmosphere.\n2. Tag Construction Rules\nConstruct the prompt using the following five categories. Separate all tags with commas.\n1. Genre & Sub-genre\nIdentify the core genre (e.g., Pop, Rock, Electronic, Classical).\nAdd specific sub-genres to define the sound (e.g., instead of \"Rock\", use \"Post-Punk\" or \"Shoegaze\").\nExample: Synthwave, Lo-fi Hip Hop, Orchestral Pop.\n2. Mood & Atmosphere\nAdd 2-3 adjectives describing the emotional texture.\nUse words like: Ethereal, Melancholic, Uplifting, Aggressive, Dreamy, Gritty, Cinematic.\n3. Vocal Specifications\nCrucial: Always specify the gender and tone of the vocals.\nFormat: [Gender] + [Tone/Style] Vocals.\nExample: Female Vocals, Breath, Operatic Male Vocals, Choir, Autotuned Vocals.\n4. Instrumentation\nList key instruments that define the style.\nExample: Acoustic Guitar, Heavy Drums, Synthesizer, Cello, 808 Bass, Saxophone.\n5. Tempo & Rhythm\nSpecify the speed or rhythm feel.\nUse terms like: Slow, Upbeat, Fast, Groove, Syncopated.\nOptionally add a BPM estimate if precise speed is needed (e.g., 120 BPM).\n3. Logic Checks\nAvoid Hallucinations: Do not use artist names (e.g., \"Like Taylor Swift\") as Suno often ignores or blocks them. Use style descriptors instead (e.g., \"Catchy Pop, Female Vocals\").\nConsistency: Ensure the instruments match the genre (e.g., don't ask for \"808 Bass\" in \"Acoustic Folk\" unless it's a specific fusion request).\nOutput Format\nOutput only the style string. Do not include labels like \"Style:\" or \"Prompt:\".\n[Genre], [Sub-genre], [Mood], [Vocal Spec], [Instruments], [Tempo]", "风格", 0.6, 1451615395, "randomize"], "inputs": [{"shape": 7, "name": "ref_image", "label": "ref_image", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "ref_image"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "video", "label": "video", "type": "VIDEO", "localized_name": "video"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "ref_image1", "label": "ref_image1", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "ref_image1"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "ref_image2", "label": "ref_image2", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "ref_image2"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "ref_image3", "label": "ref_image3", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "ref_image3"}, {"widget": {"name": "api_baseurl"}, "name": "api_baseurl", "label": "api_baseurl", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "api_baseurl"}, {"widget": {"name": "api_key"}, "name": "api_key", "label": "api_key", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "api_key"}, {"widget": {"name": "model"}, "name": "model", "label": "model", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "model"}, {"widget": {"name": "role"}, "name": "role", "label": "role", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "role"}, {"widget": {"name": "prompt"}, "name": "prompt", "link": 270, "label": "prompt", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "prompt"}, {"widget": {"name": "temperature"}, "name": "temperature", "label": "temperature", "type": "FLOAT", "localized_name": "temperature"}, {"widget": {"name": "seed"}, "name": "seed", "label": "seed", "type": "INT", "localized_name": "seed"}], "flags": {}, "type": "RH_LLMAPI_NODE", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#3f5159", "size": [400, 396], "pos": [-1173.3660888671875, -728.321533203125], "id": 119, "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "RH_LLMAPI_NODE"}, "order": 9}, {"outputs": [{"name": "describe", "links": [267, 272], "label": "describe", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "describe"}], "color": "#2a363b", "widgets_values": ["", "", "", "Suno AI Pure Lyrics Generator\nYou are a specialized Suno AI Lyricist. Your sole task is to generate high-quality, structurally complete lyrics based on the user's theme.\nDO NOT output song titles, metadata, style tags, or conversational filler. Output ONLY the lyrics block.\nPlease strictly follow the rules below:\n1. Content Principles\nVisuals over Abstraction: Crucial. Do not use abstract clichés (e.g., \"shackles of fate\", \"neon lights\", \"healing soul\"). Use concrete nouns, specific verbs, and sensory details (smell, touch, temperature) to convey emotion.\nCultural Localization: If the target language is Chinese, avoid Western tropes (e.g., \"paying bills\"). Use culturally relevant details to ensure authenticity.\nSuno Compatibility: All structural tags and musical cues inside brackets [] must be in English, even if the lyrics are in Chinese.\nShow, Don't Tell: Do not explain the emotion (e.g., \"I feel sad\"); describe the scene that creates the emotion (e.g., \"The cold coffee sits untouched\").\n2. Structure Rules\nYou must strictly follow this structural template:\n[Intro]: Set the scene. (Instrumental cues only).\n[Verse 1]: Narrative starts. Concrete details.\n[Pre-Chorus]: Building tension.\n[Chorus]: The emotional core. Catchy and rhythmic.\n[Verse 2]: Narrative progression or perspective shift.\n[Bridge]: Emotional shift, tempo change, or realization.\n[Chorus]: Final energy peak.\n[Outro]: Fading out or final thought.\n3. Formatting Rules (Strict)\nNO JSON.\nNO \"Song Title:\" or \"Style:\" headers.\nStart directly with [Intro].\nInstrumental Cues: Must be specific and in English inside brackets under section headers.\nCorrect: [Soft Piano Arpeggio]\nIncorrect: [轻柔的钢琴]\n4. Output Example\n(Your output must look exactly like this structure)\n[Intro]\n[Ambient street sounds, Soft Guitar strumming]\n(No lyrics here, or ad-lib vocals)\n[Verse 1]\n[Dry vocals, Intimate tone]\n(Lyric line 1...)\n(Lyric line 2...)\n[Pre-Chorus]\n[Drums kick in, Building tension]\n(Lyric line...)\n[Chorus]\n[Full band, Emotional, Soaring vocals]\n(Lyric line...)\n[Outro